BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 498.65 Tm (Step: 4) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 483.42 Tm (Title: Arm the Rerouting Rules) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 468.20 Tm (Action: Turn on busy-signal rerouting, a short ring timeout and duplicate routing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 452.97 Tm (for repeat callers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 437.75 Tm (Detail: Ringba checks in milliseconds whether the person has called before and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 422.52 Tm (routes them to buyer two, which has no relationship with that caller and treats it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 407.30 Tm (as fresh [Ringba - ojcbZuG798w @ 00:16:51].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 385.07 Tm (Mattias Mesters walks through the core routing plan math in Ringba: priority one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 369.85 Tm (targets are always tried first, priority two only when none of them is available,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 354.62 Tm (and within a tier the weights become fractions, so targets weighted 1, 6, 6 and 1) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 339.40 Tm (split traffic 1/14, 6/14, 6/14 and 1/14 [0eCCbtHmCJE @ 00:02:34]. Error) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 324.17 Tm (handling sits on top. Adam describes Ringba detecting a busy signal within a few) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 308.95 Tm (milliseconds and immediately dialing buyer two, fast enough that no caller can) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 293.72 Tm (notice, which neutralizes call centers that oversell capacity to many publishers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 278.50 Tm (and then busy-signal overflow so they never pay for it [ojcbZuG798w @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 263.27 Tm (00:05:07]. For buyers who let calls ring 30 seconds instead of bouncing them,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 248.05 Tm (the fix is a ring timeout configured at the buyer or target level, maybe five) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 232.82 Tm (seconds, maybe ten, after which the call is pulled and rerouted [ojcbZuG798w @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 217.60 Tm (00:08:15]. Adam pairs that with a commercial term: if a ringing buyer imposes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 202.37 Tm (duration requirements, bill on duration from the moment the call starts ringing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 187.15 Tm (rather than from answer, because the buyer captured the option value of picking) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 171.92 Tm (up the whole time [ojcbZuG798w @ 00:06:38]. Adam actually prefers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 156.70 Tm (busy-signal buyers, since the bounce arrives in real time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 141.47 Tm (Simultaneous dialing rings every eligible buyer at once, whether three or 600,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 126.25 Tm (and the first to answer wins the call, but Adam flags the trap: if buyer one pays) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 111.02 Tm ($10, buyer two $22 and buyer three $6, and buyer three always answers fastest,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 95.80 Tm (sim-dial gets expensive, and mixed West Coast and East Coast requirements) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 63.00 80.57 Tm (break it too [ojcbZuG798w @ 00:11:41]. The ideal setup is nationwide buyers) Tj ET
